# PAHARA — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, or paste into Vercel's
# Project Settings → Environment Variables for a deployment.
#
# Both are optional. Without them the app runs normally and the alerts panel
# shows a "Configure Telegram" notice instead of the dispatch button.

# Bot token from @BotFather, e.g. 123456789:AAExampleTokenFromBotFather
VITE_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=

# Destination chat. A group/channel id is usually negative, e.g. -1001234567890.
# Get it by adding the bot to the chat and reading
# https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
VITE_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# SECURITY NOTE
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build time
# and is readable by anyone who opens the deployed site. That is acceptable for
# a hackathon demo with a throwaway bot; it is NOT acceptable for a real
# deployment. In production, put the send behind a server or serverless
# function that holds the token, and have the browser call that instead.
